🎯 Interview Explanation Guide

When asked about the tech stack:
"I built this Snake game using Python as the primary language with Tkinter for the GUI. The game uses Canvas widgets for rendering graphics and implements file I/O operations for persistent data storage like high scores and player names."

When asked about key challenges:
"The main technical challenges were implementing smooth snake movement where each segment follows the previous one, precise collision detection for walls and self-collision, and managing game state transitions. I solved these using coordinate-based algorithms and proper state management."

When asked about the architecture:
"The game follows a modular design with separate functions for different responsibilities - movement, collision detection, scoring, and UI management. This makes the code maintainable and allows for easy feature additions."

When asked about data structures:
"I used lists to store the snake body segments and food items, canvas objects for visual representation, and text files for persistent data storage. The leaderboard uses sorted lists for ranking players."

When asked about scalability:
"The modular design allows easy addition of new features. The file-based storage can be upgraded to a database for better performance, and the canvas-based rendering supports visual enhancements."

